sceNpSignaling: connections for Matching2 room members; context ids from 1; ActivateConnection

On the console Matching2 connects room members through sceNpSignaling, so a member's connection has a sceNpSignaling
id and its ESTABLISHED / DEAD events reach every context's handler and extended handler, besides the Matching2
signaling callback. Here the member events went only to the Matching2 callback, context ids started at 0 (read by
titles as no context), and ActivateConnection was an offline stub.

Now: context ids are slot + 1. One connection per peer online id, with the address and P2P port from the psnr member
record and its status from the member events and ActivateConnection (PENDING until the member is up). When the peer's
side is up and this side has activated it, the extended handler also gets EXT_PEER_ACTIVATED and
EXT_MUTUAL_ACTIVATED. GetConnectionStatus, GetConnectionInfo (by code), GetPeerNetInfo and the new
GetConnectionFromNpId answer from the table. The event values follow the SDK (DEAD 0, ESTABLISHED 1, NETINFO_ERROR 2,
NETINFO_RESULT 3, EXT_PEER_ACTIVATED 10, EXT_PEER_DEACTIVATED 11, EXT_MUTUAL_ACTIVATED 12), and GetConnectionInfo
takes its code argument. RTT and bandwidth are fixed placeholder values (1 ms, 10 Mbit/s) until psnr measures them.


